# Agent-authored, append-only logs. Parallel lanes only add new dated entries, so
# concatenating both sides is always the correct merge and Git resolves it without
# a conflict. Never list a file here that agents edit in place: union merge would
# silently keep both versions of a rewritten line.
#
# Union is the safety net, not the strategy. The owner prompt log is split per lane
# under docs/reference/owner-inputs/prompts/ so two lanes never write the same file
# and no merge is needed at all. Prefer that pattern for any new agent-written log.
docs/reference/history/requirements-log.txt merge=union
docs/reference/owner-inputs/prompts_executed.txt merge=union
docs/reference/owner-inputs/prompts_executed_imp.txt merge=union
docs/reference/owner-inputs/prompts/*.txt merge=union whitespace=-trailing-space
docs/ENGINEERING_LEARNINGS.md merge=union

*.command text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
